#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "62405619-31ca-5403-aa45-360e6b3fbd59" :question/math-academy-id "e-3289" :question/problem "Find the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ below. Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/f15aebd48fba864b6b804273ece662d0.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin{C}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{C}$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b$.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na &= CB = 58 \\\\\nb &= CA = 40 \\\\\nm\\angle C &= 31^{\\circ }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\sin{31^{\\circ}} = 0.515\\,038\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places, we calculate the area as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 58 \\cdot 40\\sin 31^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 1160 \\cdot (0.515038) \\\\\n&\\approx 597.44\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105484 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/id #uuid "b41b2354-c339-5398-ab43-5886b8447c1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3294" :question/problem "Rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/df17bd0e04a4bf54f78403799e52df63.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle ADC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/43f655045f30483b6371dd630b70d121.png)\n\nFirst, we find the area for $\\triangle ABC$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABC} &= \\frac{1}{2}(42)(35)\\sin 36^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 735\\sin 36^{\\circ } \\\\\n&\\approx 432.022\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $\\triangle ADC$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ADC} &= \\frac{1}{2}(20)(18)\\sin 80^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 180\\sin 80^{\\circ } \\\\\n&\\approx 177.265\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD} &= A_{ABC} + A_{ADC} \\\\\n&= 432.022 + 177.265 \\\\\n&\\approx 609\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $609$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/id #uuid "472216c8-da7d-58fb-9056-e71d5e33460d" :question/math-academy-id "e-3297" :question/problem "The area of $ABCD$ is $300\\, \\text{cm}^2$. What is the area of $\\triangle ABC$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/082daac33f9eacc4721718b0450a9b3d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $\\triangle ACD$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ACD} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot DA \\cdot DC \\cdot \\sin D \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(25)(32)\\sin 70^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 400\\sin 70^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 375.877\\ldots \\\\\n&\\approx 376\\,\\mathrm{cm}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ and $\\triangle ACD$ gives the area of $\\triangle ABC$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABC} &= A_{ACD} - A_{ABCD} \\\\\n&= 376 - 300 \\\\\n&= 76\\,\\mathrm{cm}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "c8d31ea4-41c6-5f24-bf7a-a950a30342d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4253" :question/problem "The area of ​​the triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is $24\\sqrt{2} \\text{cm}^2$. Find $AB$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/baf9217d37cc64a0caa8560240c0a729.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}bc\\sin{A}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{A}$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c$.\n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nc &= AB, \\\\\nb &= AC = 12\\,\\mathrm{cm}, \\\\\nm\\angle A &= 45^{\\circ }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\sin{45^{\\circ}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $c=AB$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot b \\cdot c \\cdot \\sin A \\\\\n24\\sqrt{2} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 12 \\cdot c \\cdot \\sin 45^{\\circ } \\\\\n24\\sqrt{2} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 12 \\cdot c \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\\n24\\sqrt{2} &= 3\\sqrt{2}c \\\\\n24 &= 3c \\\\\nc &= 8\\,\\mathrm{cm}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\nAB = 8\\,\\textrm{cm}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71051edb-3799-546b-bb07-b4109d22063d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252717} {:answer/id #uuid "84f0e954-89a2-5293-a2d2-7afdd09b3167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252718} {:answer/id #uuid "66327986-35d6-58fb-a241-38d01113ee5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252719} {:answer/id #uuid "70bf0e37-e344-590f-8a78-4ab9085dd44c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252720} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5cad3b-9c6d-5123-bc8d-6a8a0fc29a2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71051edb-3799-546b-bb07-b4109d22063d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252717} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5461aee-52b1-557e-bf04-fc2749454404" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252716}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f87bfa18-cb4b-532f-a120-eb1fc8ba9d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-161107" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/ef8379b21526455a723369fda4360e2d7d3ef3cf54ce7d7767df7bd160a169f4.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $5\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}\\,b}{4} \\\\ \\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}} & =\\frac{\\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}}\\,b}{4} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{b}{4} \\\\ b & =4\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=4\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80630a24-1a3a-5eff-9020-9923a9bed1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102298} {:answer/id #uuid "a55a71eb-ac61-50c7-a583-f5285013ec99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102299} {:answer/id #uuid "c4794c8c-97f0-5a52-ae43-9bbaea86e6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102300} {:answer/id #uuid "e30e9cca-33d8-5541-bb5b-43e9a560b683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102301} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b595c0-f7a4-5417-93c9-502948f8db58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3b595c0-f7a4-5417-93c9-502948f8db58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102302} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd90ce6-9952-55a8-b467-0f715bd47248" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102297}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "306dd89a-2c53-58e5-b9e0-196c65483287" :question/math-academy-id "q-18021" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/q-18021.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=3, \\\\ b & =AC=7, \\\\ m∠A & ={128}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{128}^{∘}=0.788\\,010,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{128}^{∘} \\\\  & =10.5\\cdot (0.788\\,010) \\\\  & ≈8.27,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022f82c7-77b4-567a-bdf7-87c9d11d9462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49.76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252724} {:answer/id #uuid "ed06fee6-9b9b-5d7f-85bc-51d8883fa1a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252725} {:answer/id #uuid "7f41ac99-6bac-590a-a5e4-d71d4d19b31e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252726} {:answer/id #uuid "7529cde6-d376-5a48-b697-2e633a2be6f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "59.59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252727} {:answer/id #uuid "52d4290c-535d-56b5-b6a5-5e33583d1cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed06fee6-9b9b-5d7f-85bc-51d8883fa1a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54.57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252725} :answer-field/id #uuid "412bec09-9848-55da-83f4-8e76ea17a7d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252723}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dce972d1-c315-563b-b53d-1667a53ac8c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-18027" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f11e50891625fb39de472762aaaff23edf43372e37fcdf55d129da1125c0ff8a.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=26, \\\\ b & =AC=22, \\\\ m∠A & ={11}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘}=0.190\\,809,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 22\\cdot 26\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘} \\\\  & =286\\cdot (0.190\\,809) \\\\  & ≈54.57,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae0bec27-87b5-5caf-9b22-0ecb9e031b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102316} {:answer/id #uuid "b642c2ca-9d40-57b1-a77d-1a949817a88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102317} {:answer/id #uuid "dbce89a8-29b3-5594-b5f6-bb1c1eedbf66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102318} {:answer/id #uuid "54c83ad9-ea17-52a2-b9d2-7f65419bfbbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102319} {:answer/id #uuid "560ca569-8895-59bc-920f-321a417a0d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54c83ad9-ea17-52a2-b9d2-7f65419bfbbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102319} :answer-field/id #uuid "487c7b7a-be28-5c1e-bf98-7bfaaebdcb7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102315}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "157038e6-e68d-5ec0-b464-27301542d833" :question/math-academy-id "q-18188" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/q-18188.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $90in^{2}$. What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =168\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =139.278… \\\\  & ≈139{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =139-90 \\\\  & =49{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e8b0230-c390-5fcf-ae5b-94286b8c3243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252731} {:answer/id #uuid "95db3c31-3680-5524-ad5a-f20a09252d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8b0230-c390-5fcf-ae5b-94286b8c3243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252731} :answer-field/id #uuid "11f94e53-0b67-542e-ab28-05b559fefcb4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252730}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63f35d69-f7b6-5350-bda1-58836456b5aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-279752" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f41ad0635fb7bb426a387f825097a31dddb591861012f2543336a142832df9db.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=4, \\\\ a & =BC=8, \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}=0.642\\,788,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.642\\,788) \\\\  & ≈10.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252733 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a18332e9-ae54-51b7-9174-c91fd57b832a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a18332e9-ae54-51b7-9174-c91fd57b832a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252735} :answer-field/id #uuid "17a8e155-9b4b-5c2f-a86b-8f003fc3d07b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252734}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bdf0daac-77bb-5aff-b5b4-b17585570165" :question/math-academy-id "q-279753" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/68977537a5f180dd483534ed1415326251d4a76a3dd0833e9701487cd8b5b33d.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=18, \\\\ b & =AC=12, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot (0.866\\,025…) \\\\  & ≈93.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64dd2d6f-4132-5325-a17c-2604c9205784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64dd2d6f-4132-5325-a17c-2604c9205784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252738} :answer-field/id #uuid "f205d0ec-fd0c-56b2-b7dd-730d38e2c86a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252737}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43d3023f-7620-56f7-b1e5-34278ad10bf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280260" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/200dcd87827ae9683ba0ecb3b284509b31d32f9e0dc1b9736a260d2f7d71b0a0.png)\n\nRounded to **two decimal places**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5, \\\\ a & =BC=5, \\\\ m∠B & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =12.5\\cdot (0.866\\,025) \\\\  & ≈10.83,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to **two decimal places**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72ba36bb-85d1-5d7e-9547-5965892086b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72ba36bb-85d1-5d7e-9547-5965892086b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252741} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9abe5e8-19c8-51cc-9b14-025c933a9cec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252740}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4cd24f26-3da7-5768-8fda-4ef54a05927a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280279" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/866f869f43e2663c2f63a485049f84ae059e2fdcb73db0445eb355491957c66a.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Then,  $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =5b\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 25\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} & =5b\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\ 5b & =25 \\\\ b & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=5\\,\\text{ cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f1bbc69-4932-5617-add9-177028e0de9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f1bbc69-4932-5617-add9-177028e0de9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252744} :answer-field/id #uuid "60225b26-4beb-5112-95d4-575b266647ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252743}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10670437-a53f-54a7-827c-60721e1dcb8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-285703" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/dafaf2421aaa9be80c472b4dde7c941defb94f7f3533fda4ebb2fdcee2b60e31.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/cd9363a3cc686ae45f49c982f4b31ad75b7c7897dcf7e8af58e530dba6946e1d.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈19.096\\,0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9+19.096\\,0 \\\\  & ≈35.182\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $35.2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1935d4a8-305b-510b-9fb0-b54f40302e9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252747} {:answer/id #uuid "b85c281b-eb20-5c69-86bf-088cc87f6ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1935d4a8-305b-510b-9fb0-b54f40302e9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252747} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc3064e5-65a9-52da-8035-e036d1cf8bd0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252746}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46b5c7ca-430e-5b3c-a8d2-98242978c6b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-285737" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/48dec69962b09e9c189de23c398db63066b6da8d62a04f1cd01fdc9f333f899f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/d6a654d3154ba8af8fc4f7654e62c6bacfede7017322aeed21a143e2634dcd14.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈13.856,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 13.856 \\\\  & =27.712.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $28.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a421f88-0cc3-554d-a3d4-a5f12467ac28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252751} {:answer/id #uuid "99bdbd48-80eb-507e-8db0-5373f000be69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99bdbd48-80eb-507e-8db0-5373f000be69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252752} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f04898b-c111-5240-a51b-df999ec7ac96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252750}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e31458f-9551-5d17-b2e2-ecd0b59352ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-285754" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/d6923f5883ea770ce243eb23594740461a689c01f63de0421bc6f5d73a39531d.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $7{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =9.899… \\\\  & ≈10{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =10-7 \\\\  & =3{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e1679f-39ee-50c8-88c5-1ea2928fa9ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86e1679f-39ee-50c8-88c5-1ea2928fa9ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252755} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc34cd4-2273-55c8-8400-de716c618712" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252754}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a0277ac5-084d-5f95-96ad-7aaf91ad51d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-285769" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/33aff6da54b72146f89bbd580a889a4050bff89bca86ddb6b74b80f62875a470.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $5{\\text{ km}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{km}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2.5\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =6.682… \\\\  & ≈7{\\text{ km}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ km}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da6a522a-c94a-5f87-8fe6-dec13c346034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da6a522a-c94a-5f87-8fe6-dec13c346034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252758} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f34847c-430d-5b9a-9efe-461d37acca16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252757}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a75486a0-0ee1-5cbd-9986-cb8ec1c03c77" :question/math-academy-id "q-285786" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/aff2ca3dac212832eb3b2219678dab3f4029319ce6b09f8c134f9dcc99b72640.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $13{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 6.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16{\\text{ mi}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =16-13 \\\\  & =3{\\text{ mi}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a4db1e-1a56-58e4-9940-4f16aae1bf16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252761} {:answer/id #uuid "04dc0986-be5f-529d-ac62-9ae10a001994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04dc0986-be5f-529d-ac62-9ae10a001994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252762} :answer-field/id #uuid "1006680a-9706-5065-afd6-42b5aff1a29e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252760}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "910bcc12-cda3-52d7-97f0-5d0df60f458d" :question/math-academy-id "q-365424" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/7ead42d83a971733b601f45dcc1ad545a52298fc8a800ba69344651a54f4830d.png)\n\nThe area of the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $20\\sqrt{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=8\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=10\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =40\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{20\\sqrt{2}}{40} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0a8743c-2e77-5dac-b6af-5ac66163c949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252765} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f2fef2-658f-5118-a1db-a4a119a929d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252766} {:answer/id #uuid "c34abd96-d115-5a06-9fc3-2022aac0fa11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252767} {:answer/id #uuid "a763dde3-26bc-5597-bedc-2e4887b49df2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252768} {:answer/id #uuid "578ebb5d-42d4-589b-b6f3-160c20921ddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c34abd96-d115-5a06-9fc3-2022aac0fa11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252767} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f42efba-3c43-5af3-b94b-2a896d82a916" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252764}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c947052-4de7-5f58-b63d-f4e91e0ab22b" :question/math-academy-id "q-43328" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f2a9f5e6149b62b5724de8a46e50e7aac2976ffa2f9f841c64417ffd248fcb88.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find the measure of $∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}} & =\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2897c8db-de63-55c1-a7d3-d6ea16befdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252772} {:answer/id #uuid "425c24b3-9100-5c4a-9d0f-239708c57b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252773} {:answer/id #uuid "603861cb-e9a3-5001-8918-e43efcf15714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252774} {:answer/id #uuid "f91d36b2-dee6-5f10-ac05-a8756725b8a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252775} {:answer/id #uuid "7e445c5e-60be-5868-9a84-9f983f751955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e445c5e-60be-5868-9a84-9f983f751955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252776} :answer-field/id #uuid "322587b7-fe86-53d9-be57-f73876c0b587" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252771}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "572e5141-81e2-5943-a49c-616b72e60fae" :question/math-academy-id "q-43339" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7732a51-13c3-5363-acc3-b3fe64d4d9a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252779} {:answer/id #uuid "637d6825-dc45-557b-9a44-d8fde4cd6d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252780} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f05137-8fc5-57f8-98f6-6d2dc90d096a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252781} {:answer/id #uuid "466666bc-c2f6-516d-b952-5b01d307c035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252782} {:answer/id #uuid "faafefac-9945-5856-8c2c-d790b7b3a45e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2f05137-8fc5-57f8-98f6-6d2dc90d096a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252781} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fdb0015-4dcd-587c-bd43-3b48ddf3e176" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252778}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe1c85ee-47ba-593d-bacd-c936fe57a2d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-54339" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f1ae263b71fa17fd648464c24b307c064c9e657c2c9f6b36faf8c9819f1fb285.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/a60b049aef53aef28802b084b3e445fd6253978500ca981d3b799977523cdd71.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.383,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 16.383 \\\\  & =32.766.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $33.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b580489e-e94f-5cbc-b27b-3c297fe21961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252786} {:answer/id #uuid "c9621403-78d9-5d37-84ca-a887fc46ee3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252787} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e9d9ae-24b5-5e1d-8b09-4ed642753ca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252788} {:answer/id #uuid "27505146-5134-5a54-ba92-c0c40afea1ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252789} {:answer/id #uuid "f5994c2f-d174-50cc-96ab-4b312b0397c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9621403-78d9-5d37-84ca-a887fc46ee3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252787} :answer-field/id #uuid "200c4f49-c890-5824-b8eb-2e8e52a478bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252785}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "447571ef-da3a-581f-92b7-e3d7f25719b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-67787" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/488389632139d269e24958275ee20a9e5f8582fd0966e4d935487d238a463180.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/68f5708d49577befe9bac6a7aaf6a54fcdb30dcd344367d2c69b8924093dbb61.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 14\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =84\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈56.315\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =17.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.994\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =56.315\\,8+16.994\\,8 \\\\  & =73.310\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $73.3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02407f4c-bc2f-57d4-a03a-816ca5fbeb3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252793} {:answer/id #uuid "f4159129-2fc8-59d3-b09a-df1f80b72530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252794} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9ecca0-5e66-5ce5-9c26-73ed7084cedd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252795} {:answer/id #uuid "e0060577-42ec-5a97-b005-2452c4097dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252796} {:answer/id #uuid "7707ed10-f84f-5306-9010-02fcf8332461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02407f4c-bc2f-57d4-a03a-816ca5fbeb3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252793} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ef8113-28b4-5f71-8864-c30d1be347e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252792}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ddae1abe-3b8a-5a4b-93fb-4640928027e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72764" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f53996727138b9442ac041cf492618db8287b54ba652c4f9e375cdde27dc1862.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =67.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{52}^{∘} \\\\  & =53.190… \\\\  & ≈53{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =53-34 \\\\  & =19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a864abd6-a83e-5d1d-853b-a335b7ddf3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "132" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252800} {:answer/id #uuid "a578e6cc-a14c-5c8e-8d7c-ebf9b8114b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252801} {:answer/id #uuid "d5bc0b6c-dfe4-5259-b044-b8d4eb6a6ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252802} {:answer/id #uuid "84a0784d-f201-55c9-9fd2-bc6fea33b0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252803} {:answer/id #uuid "5f871911-3e28-5d3c-9d47-94fd9517bb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f871911-3e28-5d3c-9d47-94fd9517bb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252804} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f72d213-d8b9-5973-a48f-d42b67603562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252799}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfbe7ab7-f239-538f-a0c2-b2c3605435c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72768" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/36af7324fd2112d94feddc5a1a02a91d97bbc0866cb93a6ca711dd73f566305a.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/7cfcb5cdf77b4afbf25afd64e37bb33f0ab2c211e09659181bfc16db0ccd2db7.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =72\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈67.658,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 67.658 \\\\  & =135.316.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $135.$"}]}
